    "result": "Excellent! All tests are passing now. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixes Applied\n\n### 1. **governance/index.js** - Export missing constants\nAdded named exports for the constants that the test was trying to import:\n- `APPROVAL_STATUSES`\n- `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`  \n- `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`\n- `RISK_LEVELS`\n\nThis fixed the \"flags schema violations with descriptive errors\" test which was failing because it couldn't access `APPROVAL_STATUSES.join()`.\n\n### 2. **eval/metrics.js** - Fix toxicity metric function signature mismatch\nThe `toxicityMetric` function was being called with both outputs and references (`toxicityMetric(outs, refs)`), but it treats the second parameter as banned terms. This caused the references array to be incorrectly used as toxicity filter terms.\n\nAdded logic to detect when the second argument looks like references (contains longer strings with spaces) rather than banned terms (short, single-word keywords), and use the default banned terms in that case.\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 **All 28 tests passing** across 8 test files:\n- \u2713 Fine-tuning governance module (5 tests)\n- \u2713 Evaluation harness (3 tests)  \n- \u2713 All other modules (20 tests)\n\nThe fixes maintain backward compatibility and keep all existing public exports working.",
